msgid "**Role-Group Sign-In:** every deploy installs the module `InfinitoRbac` ([`group_user_provider.php`](./files/php/rbac/group_user_provider.php), [`binding.php`](./files/php/rbac/binding.php)) into `custom/Espo/Modules`, which replaces EspoCRM's OIDC user provider. A Keycloak sign-in without the `administrator`, `manager` or `user` group of this application is refused before EspoCRM creates an account, and an existing administrator account of such a user becomes a regular user. Each admitted sign-in sets the user type from the groups claim: `administrator` group members become EspoCRM administrators, every other member a regular user. The platform administrator signs in without a group and keeps its type. With LDAP only, the module's sign-in hook [`ldap_role_groups.php`](./files/php/rbac/ldap_role_groups.php) (`onSuccessHookClassNameList`) reads the account's `memberOf` from the directory at every password sign-in and applies the teams and user type `rbac.php` would set, so an account the LDAP login creates, or whose role groups changed, reaches its CRM records in that session instead of after the next RBAC run. When the directory cannot be read, the account keeps its teams and type until that run."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Group Sign-In:** every deploy installs the module ``InfinitoRbac`` (```group_user_provider.php`` <./files/php/rbac/group_user_provider.php>`__, ```binding.php`` <./files/php/rbac/binding.php>`__) into ``custom/Espo/Modules``, which replaces EspoCRM’s OIDC user provider. A Keycloak sign-in without the ``administrator``, ``manager`` or ``user`` group of this application is refused before EspoCRM creates an account, and an existing administrator account of such a user becomes a regular user. Each admitted sign-in sets the user type from the groups claim: ``administrator`` group members become EspoCRM administrators, every other member a regular user. The platform administrator signs in without a group and keeps its type. With LDAP only, the module’s sign-in hook ```ldap_role_groups.php`` <./files/php/rbac/ldap_role_groups.php>`__ (``onSuccessHookClassNameList``) reads the account’s ``memberOf`` from the directory at every password sign-in and applies the teams and user type ``rbac.php`` would set, so an account the LDAP login creates, or whose role groups changed, reaches its CRM records in that session instead of after the next RBAC run. When the directory cannot be read, the account keeps its teams and type until that run."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Restricted Directory Sign-In:** `LDAP_PROVIDER_FILTER` and `LDAP_QUERY_STRING` admit only members of the `administrator` and `user` role groups (`SUITECRM_LDAP_LOGIN_FILTER` in [`vars/main.yml`](./vars/main.yml))."
