msgid "**``local.sh`` — fully local, no external GitHub.** Checks the runner containers are healthy and the DooD socket works, then ``container cp``\\ s the repo into a runner, **builds the Infinito image locally**, and deploys ``web-app-dashboard`` (all other services disabled) inside a **sealed, throwaway Docker daemon** that shares the runner’s network namespace. The sandbox is torn down on exit, so the host stack is never touched and **no GitHub/GHCR access is required**. On the update pass the heavy deploy is skipped (it is validated once on the first pass)."
