msgid "A mesh is IPv4 only, on the underlay as inside the tunnel. Each deploy resolves every endpoint a host dials with ``getent ahostsv4`` on that host, writes the first IPv4 address into ``Endpoint``, measures the path MTU against that address and subtracts the 60-byte IPv4 tunnel header. On an interface that is already up, the deploy sets that MTU on the live link as well. An endpoint name with both an A and an AAAA record therefore always dials over IPv4. A name without an A record, an unreachable resolver, an IPv6 literal endpoint or a host whose only IPv4 address is ``127.0.0.1`` fails the deploy before the interface is rendered; pass the peer’s IPv4 address as ``--endpoint`` instead. A host with an IPv4 address but no IPv4 route to the peer fails at the handshake gate. When the hub’s address changes, redeploy every spoke."
