# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk authenticates users against the central Keycloak realm via OIDC and looks up users via the Keycloak admin Web API (`keycloak_webapi` backend). OpenLDAP feeds OpenTalk transitively through Keycloak's federation."
msgstr "OpenTalk, kullanıcıları merkezi merkezine karşı otantikleştirir Keycloak OIDC aracılığıyla dünya ve kullanıcılar üzerinde görünüyor Keycloak admin Web API (`keycloak_webapi` backend). OpenLDAP yemleri OpenTalk Geçici olarak geçiş yoluyla Keycloak“Şehir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk authenticates users via OIDC and resolves invitee searches via `https://<keycloak>/admin/realms/<realm>/users?search=…`."
msgstr "OpenTalk kullanıcıları OIDC aracılığıyla otantikleştirir ve davetli aramaları ile çözer `https://<keycloak>/admin/realms/<realm>/users?search=…`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk does not open LDAP connections itself. It relies on Keycloak's LDAP federation (`svc-db-openldap` is mapped into the central Keycloak realm) and queries Keycloak's admin Web API for user lookups. This avoids dual-source-of-truth problems and keeps LDAP credentials away from the OpenTalk service account."
msgstr "OpenTalk, LDAP bağlantılarını kendisi açmaz. Bu, bağlıdır Keycloak's LDAP federasyonu (`svc-db-openldap` Merkeze haritalandı Keycloak alem) ve sorgular Keycloak's admin Web API kullanıcı aramaları için. Bu, dual-kaynak-of-gerçek problemlerden kaçınır ve LDAP bilgilerini uzak tutar OpenTalk Servis hesabı."

msgid "OpenTalk has no administrator role: controller migration `V21__remove_administrator_role.sql` removed it, and no claim grants elevated rights. The web frontend requests the fixed scopes `openid profile email`, so the `phone` scope is never requested, and the controller stores `phone_number` only when a `[call_in]` section is configured."
