# repository-ref updaters şimdi tek birleştirilmiş PR yerine etkilenen bir rol
# talep açıyor ve diff'ı en son en son karşı yeniden destekliyorlar. *main
# main main main main main main main main main main main main main main main
# main main main main main main main main main main main main main main main*
# At run time – the update jobs check out *main main main main main main main
# main main main main main main main main main* Uyarılama işlemi yerine, bu
# yüzden bir kuyruk veya durle artık ilgili olmayan değişiklikler veya
# paketler önermez. Her rol kendi şubesini alır (*Güncelleme / Güncelleme /
# Güncelleme /<type>-<role>-<date>-<fingerprint>*) Ve bir rol-skop tekrar
# kontrol ederken, *skills-lock.json* updater kasıtlı olarak tek bir PR kalır.
# See See See See See [Güncelleme akışı
# kataloğu](docs/contributing/tools/github/actions/workflows.md).
msgid "Per-role update PRs: the Docker-image-version and repository-ref updaters now open one pull request per affected role instead of a single combined PR, and they recompute the diff against the latest *main* at run time — the update jobs check out *main* rather than the triggering commit, so a queued or stale run no longer proposes already-merged changes or bundles unrelated roles. Each role gets its own branch (*update/<type>-<role>-<date>-<fingerprint>*) and a role-scoped duplicate check, while the *skills-lock.json* updater deliberately stays a single PR. See [the update workflow catalog](docs/contributing/tools/github/actions/workflows.md)."
msgstr ""

