msgid "Security: resolved all 80 open CodeQL/code-scanning alerts and added recurrence guards. Broke an unsafe import cycle in *cli/administration/deploy/development* via a leaf *env.py*; hardened *web-app-bluesky* *server.js* (cookie prototype-pollution guard, log sanitisation, HTML-escaped exceptions, ReDoS-bounded handle regex) and *web-app-baserow* SSO open-redirect handling; required TLS ≥ 1.2 in network diagnose probes; validated *actionlint* tar members against path traversal; rewrote *decidim*/*apt-purge* regexes to avoid catastrophic backtracking; anchored six Playwright URL regexes and pinned *crs-k/stale-branches* to a SHA. Guards: an *import-linter* contract, a lint requiring justified bandit *noqa*, and ruff *BLE001* as a ratchet."
msgstr "Güvenlik: Bütün bunları çözdü 80 Açık KodQL/code-scanning uyarıları ve recurrence muhafızları ekledi. Broke güvenli bir ithalat döngüsü içinde *cli/administration/deploy/development* Bir yaprak aracılığıyla *env.py*Sertleştirilmiş; *web-app-bluesky* *server.js* (Kurabiye prototip-pollution guard, log sanitisation, HTML-escaped exceptions, ReDoS-bounded handle regex) ve *web-app-baserow* SSO açık yönlendirme; TLS ≥ 1.2 Ağ tanısı problarında; doğrulama *Aksiyon* Yol traversitesine karşı ip üyeleri; rewrote *decidim*/ /*Apt-purge* Regexes felaket geri çekilmeden kaçınmak için; altı Playwright URL regexes ve pinned *crs-k /stale-branches* Bir SHA'ya. Muhafızlar: Bir *ithalat-linter* sözleşme, haklı bir bandit gerektiren bir lint *Noqa*Ve ruff *BLE001* Bir sıçanchet olarak."

msgid "Security: the identity headers are trusted unconditionally, so openresty is the only trust boundary: every front-proxy location clears or overwrites `X-Forwarded-*`. Anything that reaches the app port without passing openresty can open the owner session. That port is published on `DOCKER_BIND_HOST`, which is `0.0.0.0` under `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER`, and in swarm the routing mesh publishes it on every node. The `X-Auth-Request-*` / `Remote-User` variants are deliberately ignored so an already-authenticated client cannot inject a different identity. Logout must go through `web-svc-logout` / the oauth2-proxy sign-out, not Postmarks' own logout link, because the proxy header re-establishes the session on the next request."
msgstr ""

msgid "Security: the identity headers are trusted unconditionally, so openresty is the only trust boundary: every front-proxy location clears or overwrites ``X-Forwarded-*``. Anything that reaches the app port without passing openresty can open the owner session. That port is published on ``DOCKER_BIND_HOST``, which is ``0.0.0.0`` under ``DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER``, and in swarm the routing mesh publishes it on every node. The ``X-Auth-Request-*`` / ``Remote-User`` variants are deliberately ignored so an already-authenticated client cannot inject a different identity. Logout must go through ``web-svc-logout`` / the oauth2-proxy sign-out, not Postmarks’ own logout link, because the proxy header re-establishes the session on the next request."
msgstr ""

