msgid "This role deploys ERPNext as an Infinito.Nexus web app using the upstream ``frappe/erpnext`` single-image multi-role pattern from `frappe_docker <https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker>`__: one Docker image, different commands per container (backend gunicorn, frontend nginx, websocket socketio, scheduler, two queue workers, plus a one-shot configurator). MariaDB and Redis come from the central ``svc-db-mariadb`` and ``svc-db-redis`` providers — the three Frappe Redis logical roles (``cache``, ``queue``, ``socketio``) share one central Redis instance via DB-number split (0 / 1 / 2). Authentication uses Frappe’s built-in Social Login Key against the shared Keycloak OIDC client without an oauth2-proxy sidecar; LDAP federation and outbound SMTP via the mail server (`web-app-email <../web-app-email/>`__) are wired when their providers are present."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys ERPNext as an Infinito.Nexus web app using the upstream `frappe/erpnext` single-image multi-role pattern from [frappe_docker](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker): one Docker image, different commands per container (backend gunicorn, frontend nginx, websocket socketio, scheduler, two queue workers, plus a one-shot configurator). MariaDB and Redis come from the central `svc-db-mariadb` and `svc-db-redis` providers — the three Frappe Redis logical roles (`cache`, `queue`, `socketio`) share one central Redis instance via DB-number split (0 / 1 / 2). Authentication uses Frappe's built-in Social Login Key against the shared Keycloak OIDC client without an oauth2-proxy sidecar; LDAP federation and outbound SMTP via the mail server ([web-app-email](../web-app-email/)) are wired when their providers are present."
