msgid "`make iterate-plan [base=<ref>] [loop=auto]` prints what an iteration on a diff has to run and names every cut: each role, mode or test it leaves out, with the reason. See the [Makefile](../../../Makefile) for every parameter. Each changed path is classified: a role path seeds its role, a format-only edit reaches nothing, a changed lint directive runs the lint suite, a shared plugin, module, script or `group_vars` key reaches whatever consumes it, and an unknown path widens to every role. An edit is format-only when the Python tree, or the YAML or JSON data with every value's type, stays the same and neither side carries a comment a deploy or a deployed program reads: a `# variant-pin:` comment, a `# nocheck:` rule whose reader is not a lint (`inventory-open-subtree`, `inventory-variable`, `header-trust`, `license-declared`), a Python coding cookie or Ansible's `WANT_JSON` marker. YAML and JSON a role ships under `files/` or `templates/` must keep an identical text. A role path also runs the unit tests that name the role. A module or script that a Makefile target outside deploys (lint, test, `iterate-plan` and the like) runs lists that target in T0; one that any other target runs widens to every role, and so does an edit of the Makefile itself."
